Pragois public transport (MHD) will introduce the flea into its ticketing system on Wednesday
On Wednesday, 1 October 2008 will be set out in the history of Prasko Dopravna podnik (the Prague Transportation Agency) as the date on which the first-moving passengers in the metro, trams and buses, which, instead of having a paper ticket, will have an electronic coupon in their pocket in their pocket.
At the moment, the latter is accessible for about a hundred and a thousand people, owners of the Opencard smart card.
Passengers can purchase a coupon 30 days or 90-day coupon from 1 January 2009 and both have it registered on their smart card at the information points and the offices of the Dopravn podnik (Transportation Agency), located in metro stations Muzeum, Mostek, Nudrao Hole-ovice, Andel,
As of the past yesterday, there is also the possibility to buy coupons over the Internet on the web pages of the Dopravn podnik: www.dpp.cz.
More than four hundred people took advantage of the service during the morning.
Those who will start using the online store can definitely forget the counters at metro stations, where they had until now stalled in long queues in order to obtain paper tickets.
Indeed, they will buy their coupon via the Internet and will be registered on their Opencard card in one of the thirteen Mustska knihovna (municipal libraries).
'In these contact points, there is at the disposal of passengers a counter with trained staff, which will help those concerned with the purchase via the Internet and, in addition, will record the coupon that they have bought on their card,' says the spokesman for the Martin Opatrna project.
Apart from the libraries, it will also be possible to record electronic vouchers on the Opencard in vending machines installed in the vestibule of several metro stations.
What do these distributors look like?
They are rehearsals, reminiscent of ticket-composting machines and passengers may already have noticed them at the metro stations Roztytyly, Budjovick, I. Pavlova, Florenc and Vltavska metro stations.
'To-day, the city has five, but by the end of the year it should be eighty,' added Opatrna.
An automaton will control the coupon instead of the driver
Automating machines that are going to work from tomorrow are easy to use.
Simply introduce the Opencard smart card and the previously purchased coupon will register itself on the card.
Electronic coupons are valid from Tomor tomorrow not only in the capital, but also around the city.
Namely, in peri-urban trains and bus lines 300 to 499, used mainly by the inhabitants of Central Bohemia communes to access the capital.
'Outhorn integrated trains in Prassko integrovano doprava (Prague-integrated transport), controllers are equipped with card readers, from which they establish the temporary and zoral validity of coupons;' explained the control of Ropid's Fiplipal banknotes, which designs pragial public transport schedules.
Peri-divial buses are equipped with card readers embedded in the driver's case.
It is therefore therefore necessary not only to show the fle-chip card to the driver, but it is also necessary to place the Opencard at the place indicated on the side of the crate.
For example, the driver controls the validity of registered coupons.
