Police screening of a van in Alava province: two thousand kg of huchisch found
Five o'clock minus ten in the morning.
Traffic control of the Euskadi police (Ertzaintza) on the border of the municipality of Armanin (Alava).
Police officers arrest two occupants of a van and the latter two initiate the leak.
Its loading, more than two tons of hashish, enough to stop them.
The police chased them and arrested one of the two occupiers, a 28-year-old man, who was identified as A.J., according to information leaked by the Department of the Interior of the Basque Government.
The arrested individual was charged with drug trafficking and forgerying documents.
The incident took place when various officials of the Alava Traffic Unit carried out a vehicle control on the N-1, at the border of the Armion Commune.
They were about to shut down a van to inspect it when the driver disobeyed orders, suddenly speeded up and control began.
The police began their pursuit until the vehicle stopped two kilometers later on the aisle, where the two occupiers descended to escape into a forested area.
The Basque police eventually arrested one of the two occupants and seized the 2,278 kilograms of hashish they were carrying that they found after inspecting the junction, an Iveco Daily.
The posterior part of the vehicle was loaded with hachish bundles, after which they transferred it to a police station for an exhaustive inspection and to weigh the drugs.
In addition, the staff members noted that the registration plate had been “falsified” since it did not coincide with the one written on the registration plate of the van, which is also why they attributed an offence of forgiveness of documents to the detainee.
Ertzaintza continues its investigation to arrest the other suspect, who has managed to escape and to determine the origin of the drug seized.
The 28-year-old Detainee, A.J., was taken into custody to carry out the various procedures and will be tried within the following hours.
