What could zuschlag amp; Companion in their invoice factory?
Coming soon, on 8 October, hearings relating to the ongoing criminal procedure will begin, against J. zuschlag and his accomplices.
Politicians and accomplices are accused of swindling, in the form of a criminal organization, on a permanent and regular basis, resulting in particularly significant damage; other charges have been brought against them, such as falsification and use of forgiveness.
According to the Public Prosecutor's Office, money from subsidies was spent for personal purposes, while benefits were justified by false bills.
The money of the State and the municipalities, approximately HUF 65 million in its entirety, went to the boxes of the Fiatal Baloldal movement, on the one hand, in the pocket of certain people on the other.
Their approach, also made public by the investigating authorities, was to collect money from the subsidies obtained by issuing invoices for costs, behind which no actual benefit was provided, and thus the associations never complied with their commitments.
According to the indictment, a large proportion of the bills were false.
For the latter, they obtained invoice logbooks at the market in Jozsefvaros, while they were making the jackets in Kiskunhalas.
For the names of companies that would appear on the invoices, it was decided, inter alia, during the tours in the Northern Province of Lake Balaton, carried out by Istvan Lados, at the request of Jonos zuschlag.
According to the latter's devotion, he had to identify pensions and restaurants.
For his personal consumption, he asked for an invoice, on the basis of which they issued the other invoices which they would submit, inter alia, with the Ministry of Youth and Sports, the Ministry of Social Affairs and Labour, as well as of the Municipalité de la Capital to access subsidies.
The vast majority of the invoices were set up by Istvan Lados and his accomplice, Andros zri, which, according to our information, focused on drafting the files necessary to obtain the subsidies.
During a "search circuit", one of Lados' choices was a bistro.
According to the two invoices issued by zuschlag in 2003, this site was responsible for the restoration of a group of 90 people, members of the Biztos Pont Egyeslet association.
However, depending on what the manager said, it would have been not possible for so many people to occupy this place at the same time.
In the same way, in the summer of 2002, the invoice issued in the name of the Jobb Jobb Jovért Foundation, which would subsequently bear the name of Egy-tt to Harmadik Évezredért, was teeming with spawblests of forms and merits.
A pension in Badacsonytomaj actually had only three bedrooms, and a maximum of ten people could spend the night there, yet the bill mentioned one hundred and thirty customers.
Expirous imaginative invoice issuers also fell in excess when they mentioned Pigal Kft, also belonging to the Horeca sector. In their accounts, neither the name of Jobb J-v-ért nor the Hoppo appeared, according to information given to the Public Prosecutor's Office.
The company’s manager, Gyuz Farkas, told hvg.hu that when the public prosecutor summoned it and showed him the invoices, he immediately knew that they were forgeries.
"The name of our company and our tax number were placed in a bad place on the stamp."
He added: "Beyond the form, the fact that according to the bill, a hundred people stayed there, did not stick together either, since this establishment has only eleven rooms, which do not have as much space.
In addition, the bill also mentions meals, and our restaurant has been closed for a long time."
zealous issue-writing issuers also did not inquired about the travel agents in Budapest, which were part of their choice, but only organising trips from abroad, naively indicating stays in Hungary on bills to be paid in cash, which also runs contrary to the agency's accounting practices.
In addition, as appeared during the investigation, they also added VAT on these documents, while services relating to the travel activities, whose destination outside the European Union, are invoiced without VAT.
Similarly, the VAT rate of the four invoices drawn up in the name of the Hotel Révf-l-p to the order of Jobb Jobb Jover was incorrect, since the company's services did not bear a VAT of 25% as indicated, but a VAT of 15 per cent; in addition, the employees of the hotel issue only printed invoices, while fals were written by hand.
The Public Prosecutor's investigation reveals that the "issuers" also made mistakes by mentioning the transport of goods by road, which the company issuing the invoices could not exercise, given that its profile was investment advice.
In addition, it is also for procedural defects, such as types of inadequate invoices and mischievous miscarriages, that the invoices issued on the order of Egy-tt a Harmadik Évezredért Alap-tv-ny, of XXI.
As in Ravenna Bt. or the Kunfehert Sports Course, both of whom deny the authors of the invoices issued on their own behalf.
The forgers paid no attention either to the fact that HIB Kft., based in Nyuregyhaza, was in liquidation at a time when (in 2001) the Fiatal Virosért Egyeslet group was supposed to have a meal at their home. According to our information, it is for this reason that the liquidator of the company denies having issued this invoice.
Invoices made deliberately
Another category of issuers of invoices consists of those who were fully aware that they were required to issue fictitious invoices.
At the request of the Fiatal group Baloldal - Ifjo Szocial, has drawn up an invoice to the Order of the Egyottt a Harmadik Évezredért Foundation, for a sum of four million HUF.
According to the indictative act, Collab Kft's manager had to issue falsious invoices by one of the accused, Ludovic Gyurfi.
In the same way, the company Biogate Kft, which is currently being liquidated and which in 2003 submitted invoices to the order of the Jobb Jobb Jv-ért Alap-tv-ny, of the association Atlasz Egyes-let and the association V-r-sfenya Egyes-let, for an amount of approximately 5 million HUF,
No financial movement had taken place, either, since the invoices issued had subsequently been cancelled, but the agencies did not avoid mentioning it in their accounts.
The next category of invoice-emitting companies is that of companies directly related to the accused.
For example, the administrative delegate of the Managing Director of Delta Tria Kft., dealing with the trade in fuel and motor vehicles, headquartered in Budapest but unhosted there, was Ivon Kubatov.
In October, November and December 2005, this company issued several invoices concerning the sale of computing equipment, for an amount of approximately HUF 18.
According to the investigation, this equipment was procured by Cash Investment Kft from Kiskunhalas, which has been in liquidation since 14 September 2005.
The headmaster of this company was a man of Romanian origin, to whom Ivon Kubatov would also have sent documents in connection with the company between 2002 and 2005.
As far as we are aware, Kubatov acknowledged during the investigation that he issued invoices to the company Atlasz, Hoppa and Egyott a Harmadik Évezredért Alap-vunny, and that it pocketed their counter-value.
It was precisely at Ivon Kubatov’s request that Romanian masons created Fa-Bani Jos Faipari Kft.
In fact, none of these companies functioned, which the accused explains by the fact that they did not receive any work.
At the same time, he used these companies, since, at the request of the co-accalaureate and write-writer of the founding acts of the companies, he made invoices to their names, to the order of associations relating to zushlag, such as the Associations Atlasz and Y-Gener.
Kubatov donated a total of 15 invoices issued by Cash Investment, Delta, Fa-Bani Jos, Jos Investment and Linaxtrade, valued at HUF 14.2 million.
The Public Prosecutor's Office believed that 10 per cent of the sums indicated on the invoices and VAT went to the Kubatov pocket.
The man even used Szi-Beri Bt. to establish fictitious invoices that were used in Biztos Pont's grant application.
In January 2006, an application for a grant from the socialist party's public utility body, Toncsics Mihoyly Alap-tvunny (TMA), in January 2006.
They obtained this grant in an amount of twice HUF 500,000, but these amounts have not been used for the objectives indicated in the application.
To avoid being known, five fictitious invoices received from Works Team Kft were presented to TMA.
In fact, it was these invoices that were found during the search of the office of the Ministry of Education.
At the hearing, some of the accused will renerate the method of fabricating the invoices, as it had already done before the Public Prosecutor's Office.
What could be really interesting would be that the main accused, Jonos 'uschlag himself, decides to lift the veil throughout history.
Until now, his confession is not very detailed, and although he has repeatedly promised to redispute every detail, he has not yet done so.
The question arises as to whether it is in its own interest, or possibly the socialists would have concluded an agreement according to which in exchange for the reimbursement of a large proportion of HUF fifty-0.5 million.
Nowadays, the latter is probably annoyed, since applications for house-replacement under house arrest, on the basis of a reduction in his or her conditions of his or her conditions of detention, continually fall into the ear of a deaf person.
While those who have caused much greater harm, and perpetrators of unresponsible economic delinquities, walk freely or at least wait at their own homes for the end of the proceedings; he does not have this possibility.
The Psychology of Ranking: Why Do We Spend More Money?
At auctions, buyers tend to spend more and overestimate the commodity.
Neurological researchers at New-Yellow-Canadian University succeeded in unlocking the Neurological and Economic Bases of this known and seemingly irrational behavior.
According to their study published in the journal Science, human beings do not want to be left behind in this type of competition, such as an eBay Auction, which is why they even prefer to pay too high a price.
This research attempted to draw up a neurological schema of this kind of "game" using experimental auctions.
One of the groups of volunteers played lottery lottery, while the other group were taking part in a fun auction, while using a Functional Magnetic Resonance Resonance (FRI) process, the researchers were analyzing the active cerebral domains of experimental subjects.
In both games, participants could earn money, but during the auction, an essential part of which is the one-third-birch, the whole being under the brain stem, called striatum, moved intensively during the loss of the game.
This part of the brain, in addition to several other functions, plays a role in the "self-stimulation" mechanism of the nervous system.
This is why, according to the researchers, the rise in prices can be explained by the leak from the violent reaction of the striatum.
In support of their theories, the economists of this group of researchers pursued financial supervisory analyses.
During these, there were three groups outnumbered in the face of a partner in a variety of circumstances.
Simply informed the monitoring group about the real value of the product in question, and they thus made their betting.
In another group, they promised that if, in addition, they came out winning the game, then they would receive an additional 15 dollars as a reward.
While the third group received these 15 dollars before the auction, but the members of the group also lost this money, in case they lost the league.
The difference between these two groups is, in fact, that the emphasis was placed in one on victory, while in the other, on failure.
Producing the neurologists' hypothesis in this way, members of the players' team "against failure" were prepared for higher bets than those made by the control group and the "victory" group.
'These results cannot be demonstrated by any existing economic theory.
In fact, each of them explained the phenomena observed at auctions only by the pleasure of winning and the parade at risk.
Only neurological Imaging methods helped remove the contradiction between the two theories by now leading to a third explanation." - noted Andrew Schotter, Professor of the Faculty of Economics at the New York University.
Hepatitis: when should we consult a doctor?
Around half a billion people throughout the world suffer from chronic hepatitis B, while in Hungary chronic liver disease is among the leading causes of death.
It's an estimated one hundred bundled patients with the hepatitis virus in Hungary, but only seven thrivers are undergoing treatment, which is due to the fact that patients often don't know that they are carriers of the virus.
Hepatitis denomination is a generic name given to infections affecting the liver caused by different viruses.
There are a lot of similarities between their symptoms. Inflammation of the liver and jaundice are characteristic, but the pathogens and diseases generated differ from each other.
Hepatitis Viruses Depending on Pathogenic Genes Propagate mainly in two forms: Hepatitis A and E through the digestive tract (e.g. contaminated food or water), Hepatitis B, C, D and other viruses through blood and body fluids (permum, vaginal secretion, saliva).
For travelers, it is in any case recommended to be vaccinated against viruses A and B.
Symptoms of Hepatitis A occur two to three weeks after the consumption of contaminated food, usually accompanied by poor general condition, weakness, stomach ache and nausea.
Then develops on the skin and on the thimble of the eye a visible jaund, the stools become lighter, and the urine takes a darker color. Healing may take two to three weeks.
Around the world, every year, a million people are dying from the most serious form of this pathage, such as cancer or cirrhosis of the liver caused by Hepatitis.
The main cause is that, according to estimates, only one in ten patients receives medical treatment.
Hepatitis C can also have serious consequences: if it is untreated, it can lead to cirrhosis or liver cancer.
Most of the patients don't know about the virus, because the pathogenic gene sneezefully destroys liver cells. In many cases, the first symptoms only appear after 20 to 30 years of age.
As a result, early prevention is very important, as well as regular testing.
Contamination is much higher than the average among a population of three groups: people who had undergone a blood transfusion before 1991, drug users and tattooed them.
At the present time, 200 per cent of patients suffering from chronic type-type C-type hepatitis are estimated at 200 per cent.
Since the disease can be detected by a routine laboratory examination, it is advisable to consult your treating doctor as soon as symptoms of unknown origin are observed.
The disease can be cured, if it is detected in a timely way. The virus can be eradicated from the body, in this way the risk of infection disappears and the development of a cancer is prevented.
World Hepat Hepatitis Day, organized for the first time in 2004 by agencies representing patients from all over the world.
Its aim is to draw attention to cirrhosis of the chronic liver caused by the viruses, the causes of its development and the importance of early diagnosis of the disease.
Does those who grow in God feel less sorrow?
According to the results of recent research, religious credential would function as a kind of analgesic, which would already have helped to make the death of Catholic martyrs more bearable.
The British newspaper Telegraph published an article according to which researchers at Oxford University carried out an interesting experiment by analyzing at what level belief in God could influence tolerance to human pain.
As part of this weird-twelon experiment, 12 Catholic believers and atheists were subjected to electroshock, while each of them was observing a painting depicting the Virgo of Mary.
According to the results, Catholic Believers were able to exclude much of the suffering.
Thanks to a technique of palpating the human brain, it has also been discovered that Catholics have been able to activate the part of their brains responsible for the regulation of pain.
This analysis is the first in a series of experiments, in which Academicians, Scholars, Philosophers and Theologians participate from different sectors of the university.
More specifically, the experiment takes place as follows: an instrument emitting sparks and diffusing electroshocks is fixed to the left-hand of the experimental subject.
The researchers asked the participants of the experiment to keep a sustained look at two paintings, one being the Virgin Mary painted by Sassoferrato in the 17th-century eremi Lady painted by Leonardo da Vinci in the 15th century.
Researchers at the origin of this experiment had hoped that the view of the Virgin Mary evokes a kind of state of faith among believers, while Da Vinci's choice of painting, not very different from the former, concerned its soothing effect.
The experimental subjects spent half an hour in an M MRI scanner, and during this time received 20 electroshbrushes in four parts following each other, while at the same time looking at either religious-the-medemplated painting or the more general-themed painting.
The Catholics stated that at the sight of the Virgin Mary, they felt like "safeness", as someone who was "taking care of" and they "tightened each other, and peace invaded them".
At the sight of religious-meditical painting, they accounted for 12% less pain than when they looked at the work of Léonard.
Psychologist Miguel Farias, who himself took part in the experiment, believes that one can achieve the same effects with any other strong image among atheists, provided they find the appropriate photo.
'We should find an image to which they are reacting very positively, such as a mother or a father,' said the psychologist.
Anglican Bishop Tom Wright welcomed the research results.
'Friendly practice should change and in a lot of cases actually changes our personality,' added Wright.
After these excellent results, there remains only the question of what would be the effect on the regulation of the pain of the subjects if the believers are shown a Madonna Painted by Léonard or by a painter of the same caliber?
Is the View of a Better Quality Virous Mary to produce better results?
You're divulging about
On the occasion of its 10th anniversary, Google claims that it can be found at the bottom of people's pocket in the same way as the sky above their heads. It knows where they spent their vacations, what specialists they are consulting and what their interests are.
Yet this is not yet enough, according to Eric Schmidt, who is an influential person in society.
As for skeptics paralleling Orwell's horror vision, they don't see much of Web 2.0.
Eric Schmidt recently told the Financial Times that the main ambition of Google is to gather even more information about its users. This is necessary for the founders of Google to be able to meet their original goal that sounded as follows: "Control in a system all information from around the world."
According to the surveyed director of Google, after a ten-year period of global upheaval, they are still only at the beginning of their goals to be able to process all the information.
To the question: what's going to be in five years? Schmidt replied that he would like Google to answer questions like "what could I do tomorrow?" or "Which is the work that suits me best?" However, the software will not be able to answer that kind of question at first glimpse until the day they know enough about the users.
It is not perfectly clear for all Internet users that the words used during searches on the Internet, the IP address of the computer which launches the search and the pages then consulted by interested persons are precisely listed.
Through the Personalized Search programme launched two years ago, users can, for example, store their own research history and be able to consult what they have been looking for, what they have clicked on; thanks to this, in the long term, Recommendations, programme based on the same logic, will be able to provide much more personalised answers, and will submit products and services based on our previous declarations and registered preferences.
What happens if someone uses my data against me, if they're looking at what my job is, ask the users, who are worried seeing Google's monopoly on information.
In most of the cases it is the potential power represented by society that can acquiescate fear, and it is not remorse, the fear of punishment, the desire for freedom or the eventual revolt against the power that can create a negative reaction among netizens.
However, it is a confirmed fact that the desired terms are not only recorded, but in justified cases they are transmitted to a third party, and in such legal cases nothing protects the personal rights of netizens.
Probably the most rescisting example in recent times is coordinated action against Brazilian paedophiles, during which Google transmitted to the Brazilian government the information it had gathered on the public page called Orkut, thus allowing identification.
Human rights-based netizens were able to shout a sigh of relief last May, when Google’s arm head-on with the electronic legal protection agency EFF, proved its law in court vis-à-vis the FBI; according to the judgment handed down in the near future, Google will still not be able to be forced by any point of the constitution to divulge information about the FBI’s secret request of any kind.
(At the same time, the federal government successfully obtained some 50,000 web-based addresses and 1,000 search terms that it had won in relation to the strengthening of the Child Protection Act, passed several years ago, but at the end of the day, it did not succeed in obtaining the lists of searches of private users, nor the entire list of websites and keywords of the last two months.)
So Google’s judgment is quite contradictory: it’s sluggressed by those who fear the transmission of their personal data, because they think that their private sphere and their private domain suffer when they start using Google services, so they are attacking them in the spirit of revolving against multinational companies that are proud of their conservative image.
During this time, American geek culture and "wilders" bringing together enthusiasts, activists and enthusiastic computer users who appear in many other countries see Google the next generation of big companies, "plug corporate", as opposed to its rival, Microsoft, categorized as an invader of the world because of Windows, even if both are fighting for the same goal.
This can be explained by the fact that Google, unlike Microsoft, doesn't queue its users with an identification code, don't require any money for its applications. Documentary code and program package, continuously refreshed, has a much more accessible effect, younger and coarser, faced with the practicing of the official software giant.
The reason may also be that geeks see very exactly the problematic relationship between human rights and the Internet, and what Web 2.0, the most proclaimed key word of recent in recent years, takes right behind it.
In fact, Web 2.0 does not concern anything other than collaboration, the fact that we intentionally leave traces behind us, and that we use the communication channels made at our disposal, and while their dimension changes one by one, the essentials remain the same: we are exposed.
A young person, in general, can maintain a profile on several public pages, from Facebook to Xanga, and it can even link them to other performances, such as Twinter, or last.fm, listing its musical habits.
While we can see many examples, such as that of the girlfriend who easily understand at the sight of the morning photos, taken by the circle of mutual friends, with whom his unfaithful friend spent the evening, or that of the company who laid off one of his employees, just for the sincere opinions that he wrote on his blog about top management, we can be sure of one thing: the term privacy is totally reconsidering.
Whoever lives an on-and-cline life is made up of what it shows for itself, and that is how one can define the principle hidden behind the behaviour of young people of today.
It wants to hide something, or at least, wants to try to bypass Google’s monopoly, can do it (starting, for example, with Scroogle, using the Google Search System, but, at the same time, intentionally leaving no trace).
The number of people who deliberately don't record themselves on public pages so that it's not possible to find them isn't the slightest. Google online services, through word-telling to image-transprocessing, to reading information can be replaced by alternative versions that aren't attached to huge server parks and don't assembling our best profile.
Published by public opinion awaits, unhappily, the moment when Google unveils its true nature.
The company is worth more than IBM (140 Billion Dollars), Intel (124 Billion Dollar) or Coca-Cola (USD 110 billion). AdWords/AdSense Advertising Domains threaten the turnover of Advertising agencies, while the services introduced at an increasing speed cause serious headache not only to Microsoft, but to many other creators.
However, critic observers find, in addition to all this, contradictions having worrying effects: for example, the top management of the company has refused, in its entirety, the protests of the employees, after it has doubled the price of prestigmonary enterprises and after the company has deemed too expensive the daily multiple restoration, taken at any time.
According to one of the company's internal rules, the new services aren't advertised only when they can be used. What's sure is that in the coming months and next few years, they're going to move the world on new points. While some people think that Google's book and archiving books and magazine archiving takes such important dimensions that society will soon find itself in front of the Supreme Court of the United States.
The fact that Google mounts a genetic database can give a good raw material to the next generation of science fiction writers. Cory Doctorow, written with Orwellian half-tunches, describes the future in which a man could be approached frighteningly through Google's data.
