accidents in the workplace, Napolitano: "Crucial Prevention"
Every day there are 2,500 accidents at work in Italy, 3 deaths and 27 who remain permanently incompulsory.
In 2007, the Inail data confirm that white deaths were about 1,200.
Figures that indicate the seriousness of the phenomenon, which remains one of the main causes of death, and causes almost twice as many deaths as homocym.
In order to receive the attention of institutions, social forces and public information on this dramatic aspect, the Anmil today, in all the Italian provinces, celebrates the 58th National Labour Accident Residency Day, institutionalized on the second Sunday of October.
