Paul Krugman's Nobel in Economics.
The Nobel Laureate in Economics was awarded to Paul Krugman for his research on business models and the localization of economic activities.
Krugman, a 55-year-would, is a Neo-Keynsian who teaches at Princeton University and is also a famous columnist for The New York Times.
Krugman is one of the greatest critics of the Bush administration’s foreign-economy and foreign-policy solutions.
A few months after the attacks in September 2001, during Enron’s days, Krugman wrote, in an article published on The New York Times, that the second event would have been more decisive than the first, in terms of implications for the history of the United States.
A prediction that unleashed many controversies, and was repulsed by the economist for years, but has now proved true.
'I'm amazed and even a little shocked about the speed of reminiscending scandals such as the collapse of Enron or Worldcom, disappeared from the attention of the audience,' Krugman said at the end of 2002.
According to Lorenzo Bini Smaghi of the European Central Bank’s Executive Committee, Krugman is an “great-value economist,” but also a highly agile divulger, which is particularly criticistic toward the Bush administration’s excess liberalism.
Open Office, this is the third edition "anti-Microsoft"
It's OpenOffice.org.3.0, the open-managing suite of personal productivity, which aims to reach even more users, from home to office, from professionals to public administration, offering a free alternative to the most notorious Microsoft Office.
As a result of almost a one-year work, carried out by volunteer developers, monitored by SUN Microsystem, the new Open Office package shows itself to the general public with a variety of novelties: from the welcome screen, and the republished and less austere interface, to others more important, such as compatibility born for the Apple Mac OS X operating system, and the support for the new ODF (Open Document Format).
Open Office paid particular attention to the interaction with the 2007 Office suite, and it is indeed possible to open the documents with the new extension of Microsoft (.docx, .xlsx, .pptx.
Also of interest, certain functions specific to specific to certain modules, such as that which make it possible to reduce the dimensions of the PowerPoint presentations, which is useful for sending them by e-mail, or for importing PDF files into the graphic development module, retaining the original appearance of the page.
Always on this forehead, it is possible to create "Hybrious PDF" documents that unite the graphic typical of the Adobe format with the elements of a spreadsheet.
Collaboration between several people is an element which has had various improvements within the applications: in the spreadsheet, various users can intervene, avoiding conflicts over modifications, in the preparation of texts, because to each collaborator is assigned a commenting colour for better recognition in the revision phase.
Some companies are even in the process of working to bring some OpenOffice functions on the Cloud, and in the next few weeks they are expected to deliver the final result.
The Italian version can be unloaded from http://it.openoffice.org/download/3.0.0/download300.html and is in addition to the English version on the mirror since Friday.
In addition to Windows and Mac OS, the sequel is, as usual, also available, for the Linux operating system.
Upon request, the installation cd may be shipped at home or in the workplace.
And if the issue of free education can be a means of disseminating it in houses, it is precisely in the business that Open Office the continuation tries the great challenge, which can already rely on various projects carried out in public administration and schools.
Not to mention the realities that offer training, consultation and assistance, ideal for small and medium-sized enterprises, which could, moreover, be opened up to business foresight.
Open Office consists of five main modules: Writer, for Word Equivalent Writing Video; Calc is the spreadsheet that aims to replace Excel; Impress, for rival PowerPoint layouts; Dbase, like Famous Access, is the program that makes it possible to work on databases; finally Drwa is the graphics module.
Target for 2008, reaching 5 million downloads, and considering today almost 3 million and 600 bundlers, it is likely that with the release of the new version, we can even surpass the expected figure
Kohl is also positive, this is the fourth case of doping.
New case of positivity in the last Tour de France: it is the Austrian of the Gerolsteiner team, Bernhard Kohl, qualified third, and winner of the jersey jersey for Best Shopper.
It is the site of the daily newspaper L'Equipe which reports the news.
At the age of 26, Kohl is the fourth positive cyclist in Cera, the third-generation Epo, after the Italian Riccardo Riccano and Leonardo Piepoli, and German Stefan Schumacher of Gerolsteiner.
The blood tests carried out on Kohl test tubes are among those carried out in recent weeks by the laboratories in Lausanne and Chatenay-Malabry.
If non-analysures confirm Cera positivity, the Eurichian will lose his third place on the lak and will necessarily have to expect two years of elimination.
The news of Kohl positivity at the third-strengthening Epo was confirmed by the head of the French anti-doping agency Pierre Bordry, who communicated to the Associated Press, having notified positivity to the Austrian authorities.
Twenty-year-year-old Authorian placed himself on the podium behind Spanish Carlos Sastre and American Cadel Evans, sweeping the pea jersey for Best Shopper.
IMMIGRES:NEW YORK IT REQUESTS IF THE ITALY IS RACITS?
Italy 'as countries of emigraneans has recently been transformed into a preferred destination for illegal immigrants" reluctantly welcomed.
Would it transform Beautiful country into a nation of racists? This is the New York Times, which dedicated a long article discussing the theme of racism in Italy, starting from the case of the young Abdul William Guibre, from Burkina Faso, killed last month in Milan for stowing a dotter of biscuits.
This case highlights what the The New York Times defines as the 'paradox of the north': the Nordic regions are both those where "more integration and more work", but also "a strongest anti-immigrant sentiment in the country and the greatest support for the Northern Lega."
To connate the increasing tension between Italians and Immigrants, the NYT also made reference to episodes of intolerance in Milan, Parma, Rome, Ciampino and Castel Volturno.
Not only.
Even the new Lega legislature to curb immigration and facilitate the expulsion of illegal immigrants is cited as proof of climate change in Italy.
Trend highlighted by the Pope and the President of the Republic: "Giorgio Napolitano during his meeting with Benedict XVI at the Quirinal called for the State and the Church to work together to overcome racism."
Suggests from expensive rent, up to EUR 900 for a bedroom.
The student rental market does not have a crisis
According to Sunia's most recent survey, the tenants' union, renting a single room can cost a student, up to 900 euro in Milan, 700 in Florence, 650 in Naples, 600 in Rome.
'The phenomenon has now reached very serious aspects to the point of excluding entire categories of young people from the right to be studied because of the very high overall costs that families of origin have to support - explains the head of Sunia's research office Laura Mariani in these cities, the strong demand from students has distorted the market so much that a process of widespread increase has begun for the residents.
In most of the cases, leasing offers also include a series of violations: non-recorded, unrecorded type-of-receivable contracts and subleasions.
For the Sunia, extraordinary interventions through the revision of the tax tax are necessary to calm prices.
Reading the investigation in detail, we see that in Milan, for a bed in the Brianza area, it takes about EUR 450; for a single room, it ranges from EUR 650 (Nere Band zone), to an average value of EUR 800 (Lomate zone, Udine and Fiera) to a maximum of EUR 900 (Vittoria area).
In Florence, one bed costs on an an average of EUR 350/400, a room around EUR 700.
In Bologna, where students are concentrated in areas close to the university, it takes EUR 250/280 for a bed in a double bed and from 370 to 500 for a single bed.
In Rome, in areas close to central universities (San Lorenzo, Piazza Bologna), about EUR 600 is requested for a single, 450 for a bed in a double.
Sparsely lower values (EUR 550 for a simple) for areas close to other universities (Ostiens and Cinecittà).
You can only be saved by moving away in peripheral areas: EUR 300 for one bed and EUR 450 for a single in the Predestina, Centocella or similar area.
In Naples, for one bed it takes EUR 300/400, for a single, we spend between EUR 400 and 600, with higher prices in Policlinico, Vomero and Colli Aminei areas.
In Bari, for a bed, it takes EUR 250/350, at least EUR 350 for a single.
In smaller cities, prices are lower in absolute terms, but they are of major importance in the urban economy.
Finally, cities such as Perugia, in which rentals are often carried out by non-Community students, there is a subsequent an anomaly: the rent charged to foreign students is increased by 25/30 per cent compared with that applied to Italians.
Far-and-your-old Paradiso Cinema, the cities eliminate the historical halls.
Historical Cinema Cinema Clothes in favour of Multiplex.
"City without movie theaters is a blind city, it's like an eyeless face"
The image offered by director Giuseppe Tornatore is an example of what's going on in Italy's major urban centers, but also in provincial cities.
The process of marginalization of the cinemas, with the emergence on the periphery of the large multi-rooms, and the death of mono-theathiorgiary in the central areas of the cities, is one of the major events that seems inevitable and undisputed; it also has all the characteristics of a true cultural crime.
Disappearing, they are often historic and memory-laden places, "It's as if one of my friends were disappearing, someone that we know, with whom we shared a bit of path and so many emotions," observed the director of Nuovo Cinema Paradiso, a film that offers Tornatore in 20 years, the first Oscar as well as the Grand Prix of the Cannes Jeury.
The figures supplied by Anec, the main association of shopkeepers, mean anything: in the last five years, 316 cinemas of the traditional type have closed, and it is the rooms of the main cities that have mainly paid the costs: 10 fewer in Florence, 9 in Milan, Naples, Bologna and Rome, 6 fewer in Turin, 5 in Palermo.
Among the regions most affected by the closure, Emilia Romaine is in the lead with 82 single-the-n cinemas lost, followed by Tuscany (44) and Lombardy (41).
Proof that the first person in charge of their disappearance is the advent of the multiplex, because it is indeed the three Italian regions that have recorded the most new multi-room cinemas: 195 more screens in Lombardy over the last five years, in Tuscany as in Emilia-Romagne.
'Italian exploitation has grown irrationally,' notes Paolo Protti, President of Anec, "it is useful to build new structures, but it would still be necessary to guarantee the survivor of those that already exist, because when a room closes in a city, these frequentagers are not necessarily willing to go to the multiplex.
Regardless of the failed deliberation of credit in favour of merchants: the state's anterior debt is about EUR 10 million.
Shamelessness is shameful that, from an ethical and moral point of view, the Government does not comply with existing laws.
In order to support the sector, it would take between EUR 16 and EUR 18 million per year.
Note the case of Bologna, the first Italian city which, worried about these closures, decided to resolve the situation by signing a protocol between Mairie and Anec, the first of its kind in Italy, to defend and promote single-the-shelter cinemas from historical centres and on the periphery.
Among the planned standards, there are tax-care facilitation measures in favour of managers and advantages for the public in terms of mobility: spectators will be able to enter the restricted traffic area, and will have special rates for parking and in certain car parks.
'This is an initiative that pleases me,' observes Giuseppe Tornatore, 'and I hope that other cities will follow Bologna, setting up other measures.
It is clear, however, that, in order to contrast the super-strengthening of multiplexs, traditional rooms must also improve the quality of sound and image, because today's audience is more demanding.
Defending traditional cinema is a theme that for me has always been an important issue: the closure of Bagheria Supercinema, the place of my teen and adolescence, was the spark that persuaded me to do "New Paradiso Cinema" that I had been thinking for 10 years.
I've been living in Rome for 25 years, and when I pass the Rialto, or Via Nazionale Quirinal, now closed, where I've experienced so many shared emotions, I turn to the other side so I don't see the panels blackened by dust.
Links between politics and 'ndrangheta, Arrest Mayor of Gioia Tauro.
“The mayor of Gioia Tauro was willing to standardize the Mayine's choices to the interests of the Piromalli clan.”
heavy accusations were made by the magistrates of the Anti-Mafia Directorate of Calabria against the Mayor and Vice-Mayor of Gioia Tauro, Giorgio Dal Torrione and Rosario Schiavione and the mayor of Rosarno Carlo Martelli, who had been arrested this morning for an external competition for Mafy association.
The levers for Gioacchino Piromalli, the former mediator between the clan and the public administrations, and his little-son lawyer, including the boss, already condemned for a maficious criminal association, as well as paying EUR 10 million.
"an affront to legal and moral standards, and above all of common-sense," the prosecutors wrote, the two local administrations had expressed a willingness to pay consultations to Master Piromalli.
"Thus it would have been granted to the co-cup - write the judges - to enter officially inside the town halls facilitating the already considerable possibilities of controlling and orienting the public administration
The chairman of the Calabrian regional committee Agazio Loiero does not only hide 'collusions between local committees and organised crime, there is more than one' in his region: 'there are places where Mafia intensity is stronger than in others, where collusion is almost inevitable.
But there are also a lot of politicians who are resisting the pressures of the ndrangheta, heroes who are honest."
This Morning’s arrests follow those last July, after which the police claimed to have beheaded the Piromalli clan.
As early as the end of last April, Gioia Tauro Municipal Council had been dissipated; already in 1991, and still because of alleged conditions between organized crime and the local administration, local politicians had been relieved of their function of administering the City.
Giorgio Dal Torrione, Mayor of UDC at the time of its dissolution, had been appointed leader of a centre-right coalition, following the May 2006 bundling.
He screamed in scandal when the prefecture commanded the dissolution of the communal council.
He accustomed Deputy Minister of the Interior at the time, Marco Minniti, accustoming him for tampering for a political issue, but in view of the request for incarceration signed this morning, the judges explained that the Piromalli clan had even managed to request the variation of the A3 project.
Starting from interceptions ordered against Dal Torrione, the pm wrote, emerged "the readiness to marry the demands of a businessman, representative of a more well-known group, close to the Piromalli, standardising the choices of the public administration to the interests of the clan.
When the energy comes from the waves, now the big ones get started.
This is an disproportionate deposit that occupies more than 70 per 70 per cent of the world's surface area, and now the world's leading energy companies are discovering it.
Waves, currents, tidals, these are the new renewable sources on which colosses like Chevron laid their eyes, and now are trying to put their hands on them.
The possibility of obtaining energy from the movements of the sea has been studied for 100 years now, and in the 1970s, in tandem with the first oil crisis, research has intensified.
When the price of oil fell, around 1980, the idea of exploiting marine energy was put aside, but now the environmental authorities and the new increase in oil give the sector a great boost.
The World Energy Council (WEC) in London estimated in 2007 that 15% of the world's electricity requirement could be covered by marine swell operating systems.
This quantity would be double the quantity produced by nuclear power plants.
In addition, there would be currents and pulsations.
Attellection pits.
The first venture on marine energy was the Enersis, which in 2005 simulated an agreement to build an installation in northern Portugal.
When the understanding was announced, it seemed like a real revolutionary pitch.
At two years of that age, more and more candidates among these companies, which have always been doomed to traditional energy, rely on marine energy.
'Chevron is currently looking at ocean energy technologies - said the spokesman of a company associated with the US oil cosy, the economic daily Wall Street Journal - and she assesses the possibilities to cooperate with us.
The co-cooperation in question relates to obtaining a deliberate permit by the United States Energy Commission, which is necessary to give rise to a marine energy exploitation project in Alaska.
This is a very interesting signal, especially considering precisely in Alaska, the Usa continues to extract oil, and recently President Bush has put in place a project for further excavations
Besides Chevron, there is Verdant Power Inc. From New York and Ocean Power of New Jew, which cross the energy path from the sea, and the sums invested so far, although their details are not well known, according to observers, an increasing interest.
Tecnology to be developed.
The experts talk about technology still in its inexperience, due to the fact that marine energy does not dissipate fears about the environmental impact.
At the present time, systems such as those of Portugal, or some in Scotland, are of a small size and do not seem to create a big problem for the ecosystem.
To produce energy on a large-scale scale, however, it is necessary to use technologies with a superior environmental impact.
'And choices are diverse: Ocean Power, e.g., uses a buoy system connected to each other.
Wavelength, which causes the bulbous to move upwards and downwards, is converted into a hydraulic pressure of the pistons and cylinders inside the floats.
The pressure rotates a turbine which, in turn, supplies a generator.
The energy is sent to the shore through submarine cables.
For the time being, we have four such systems in the project phase, waiting for a single federal approval and part of the energy could be used for a military installation.
Verdant Power, on the other hand, is already producing energy for a shopping mall and car park using six submarine turbines from the East River of New York.
The movement of water during tidals rotates the blades of the turbines, creating a rotatory movement that feeds a generator.
Verdant has announced that it has a long list of customers who are waiting for the necessary permissions to draw energy.
After the pulses, the tides.
Of particular interest, they told the Institute for the Research of Electrical Energy at the moment, deserves the potential of tidals at the moment.
Although it is an intermittent phenomenon, the tidal tide is more predictable from the wind, the sun, or the waves, and therefore more reliably as a source of energy.
And it's on tidal energy that states like New York, Maine and Alaska, along with others, are looking to the tidals, have invested seven and a half million dollars in 2008 and are projecting investments of up to EUR 35 million in 2009.
